course: dictionary
lesson: 694
title: Banish: sending away and getting rid of
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Banish is a strong word, and the clues around it tell you which meaning fits. «The king had to banish the cruel traitor from the kingdom.» A traitor betrays their own country, and a king would not let him stay, so banish means send him away from the land and forbid him to come back.
explain: «Ravi tried to banish his worries by reading his favourite book.» Worries are not places, so banish cannot mean sending them away. It means get rid of them completely. Always ask: what would fit here? Get rid of fits this sentence; send away does not.
explain: «Go on, banish yourself from the kitchen before you eat all the biscuits!» Nobody is really being punished, and the speaker is probably smiling. When the tone is playful, banish means order someone to leave, as a joke. Look at who is speaking and how they say it.
fact: Banish is a verb: banish, banishes, banished, banishing.
fact: «Banish» means to send someone away from a country or place as a punishment, and forbid them to come back.
fact: «Banish» can also mean to get rid of something completely, such as a feeling or a thought.
fact: Kings in history and wizards in fairy tales often banish people, and in everyday life we banish boredom, worries or germs.
fact: Useful phrases: banish someone from a place, banish the thought, and banished to his room.
exercise: The king decides to banish the traitor. What does banish mean here? | Ask them to sing | *Send away from the land and forbid them to return | Give a big party for | Paint a picture of
exercise: «Ravi tried to banish his worries.» What does banish mean? | Share them with his dog | Make them grow bigger | *Get rid of them completely | Write them down in a diary
exercise: Which sentence uses banish as a punishment? | *«He was banished to his room for lying.» | «The fog began to banish.» | «She tried to banish the thought from her head.» | «We banish the germs with soap.»
test: «The wizard waved his wand to banish the evil spirits.» What does banish mean in this sentence? | Make them bigger | Count them slowly | *Get rid of them completely | Invite them in for tea
test: What part of speech is banish? | *Verb | Noun | Adjective | Adverb
exam: The wizard waved his wand to ___ the evil spirits from the village. | Greet | *Banish | Bake | Measure
